   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"line-height:normal;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\">I am new to Bayesian multilevel modelling and I&#39;m trying to run some very simple models but I always run into the same warning message:</p><p style=\"line-height:normal;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\"><br></p><p style=\"line-height:normal;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\">The model looks as followed:</p><p style=\"line-height:normal;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\">model1 &lt;- brm(y ~ x1+ x2 + x3 +<br>(1 | id),<br>data = data)</p><p style=\"line-height:normal;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\"><br></p><p style=\"line-height:normal;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\">summary(model1)</p><p style=\"line-height:normal;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\"><br></p><p style=\"line-height:normal;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\">Warning messages:<br>1: Rows containing NAs were excluded from the model<br>2: In if (nchar(CXX) &gt; 0) return(TRUE): the condition has length &gt; 1 and only the first element will be used</p><p style=\"line-height:normal;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\"><br></p><p style=\"line-height:normal;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\">I don&#39;t understand the second warning message. Can someone explain it to me and do I have to be concerned about it?</p><p style=\"line-height:normal;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\"><br></p><p style=\"line-height:normal;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\">It seems that the warning message does not come from the brms package itself. (All of my packages are updated). </p><p style=\"line-height:normal;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\"><br></p><p style=\"line-height:normal;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\">I very much appreciate your help.</p></div>"
